# Deployed to html/reports/_owner/.htaccess
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING HERE: on this host an .htaccess in the
# webroot is close to decorative. Two things have now been tested directly and
# both were ignored:
#
#   - Auth* directives. A correct AuthType/AuthUserFile/Require block still
#     served 200 to an unauthenticated request (verified against origin, with
#     Cloudflare reporting a cache MISS, so not an edge artifact).
#     Authentication is therefore enforced in index.php.
#   - mod_headers Cache-Control overrides, including `Header always set`. The
#     platform rewrites responses on this path to
#     `Cache-Control: public, max-age=2678400` regardless, overriding the
#     no-store the gate sends from PHP.
#
# The caching one bites: while this directory was briefly absent on 2026-09-08
# an edge node cached the 404 and kept serving it after the page was restored,
# which from the other end looks exactly like "the page doesn't exist". The fix
# that actually works is a CDN purge, so deploy_owner.py now runs one on every
# deploy. Authenticated responses were checked separately and are NOT cached -
# Cloudflare reports them DYNAMIC and the no-store header survives on them - so
# this is a staleness problem, not a disclosure one.
#
# What remains below is only what does not depend on AllowOverride for headers.

Options -Indexes
